#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Understanding high availability and disaster recovery for Quantum Compute {#understanding-high-availability-and-disaster-recovery-for-quantum-compute}"
msgstr "Entender la alta disponibilidad y la recuperación ante desastres de Quantum Compute {#understanding-high-availability-and-disaster-recovery-for-quantum-compute}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "High availability (HA) is the ability for a service to remain operational and accessible in the presence of unexpected failures. Disaster recovery is the process of recovering the service instance to a working state. IBM Quantum Compute Service customers are not responsible for disaster recovery planning or actions.\n"
msgstr "La alta disponibilidad (HA, por sus siglas en inglés) es la capacidad de un servicio de mantenerse operativo y accesible ante fallos inesperados. La recuperación ante desastres es el proceso de restablecer la instancia del servicio a un estado funcional. Los clientes de IBM Quantum Compute Service no son responsables de planificar ni ejecutar acciones de recuperación ante desastres.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum Compute is a regional service that fulfills the defined [Service Level Objectives (SLO)](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/resiliency?topic=resiliency-slo) with any paid plan. For more information, see the [Service Level Agreement (SLA)](https://www.ibm.com/support/customer/csol/terms/?id=i126-9268&lc=en) for IBM Cloud&reg;. For more information about the available IBM Cloud regions and data centers for Quantum Compute, see [Service and infrastructure availability by location](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/overview?topic=overview-services_region).\n"
msgstr "Quantum Compute es un servicio regional que cumple con los [Objetivos de Nivel de Servicio (SLO)](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/resiliency?topic=resiliency-slo) definidos en cualquier plan de pago. Para más información, consulta el [Acuerdo de Nivel de Servicio (SLA)](https://www.ibm.com/support/customer/csol/terms/?id=i126-9268&lc=en) de IBM Cloud&reg;. Para más información sobre las regiones y centros de datos de IBM Cloud disponibles para Quantum Compute, consulta [Disponibilidad de servicios e infraestructura por ubicación](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/overview?topic=overview-services_region).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "High availability architecture {#high-availability-architecture}"
msgstr "Arquitectura de alta disponibilidad {#high-availability-architecture}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "High availability features {#high-availability-features}"
msgstr "Características de alta disponibilidad {#high-availability-features}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This service is provisioned across three zones in a multi-zone region with no single point of failure. API requests are routed through a load balancer to the HA instance nodes, each in a different zone.\n"
msgstr "Este servicio se aprovisiona en tres zonas dentro de una región multizona, sin ningún punto único de fallo. Las solicitudes de API se enrutan a través de un balanceador de carga hacia los nodos de instancia de HA, cada uno en una zona diferente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If an HA instance node or zone fails, the service continues to run API requests through to the surviving HA instance nodes.  No noticeable degradation of service occurs during a zonal failure.\n"
msgstr "Si un nodo de instancia de HA o una zona falla, el servicio sigue procesando las solicitudes de API a través de los nodos de instancia de HA restantes. No se produce ninguna degradación perceptible del servicio durante un fallo zonal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is available in the following regions:\n"
msgstr "Está disponible en las siguientes regiones:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Washington DC (us-east)\n"
msgstr "Washington DC (us-east)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Frankfurt (eu-de)\n"
msgstr "Frankfurt (eu-de)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Disaster recovery {#disaster-recovery}"
msgstr "Recuperación ante desastres {#disaster-recovery}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Disaster recovery (DR) covers the steps required to restore IBM Quantum Compute Service to a working state after a regional failure or other major incident.\n"
msgstr "La recuperación ante desastres (DR) abarca los pasos necesarios para restablecer IBM Quantum Compute Service a un estado de funcionamiento tras un fallo regional u otro incidente grave.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM responsibilities {#ibm-responsibilities}"
msgstr "Responsabilidades de IBM {#ibm-responsibilities}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM is responsible for the following disaster recovery tasks:\n"
msgstr "IBM es responsable de las siguientes tareas de recuperación ante desastres:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Restoring or rebuilding the provisioning environments and resources in the affected region.\n"
msgstr "Restaurar o reconstruir los entornos y recursos de aprovisionamiento en la región afectada.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Automatically recovering and restoring IBM Quantum Compute Service capabilities to normal operations following a regional or major incident.\n"
msgstr "Recuperar y restablecer automáticamente las capacidades de IBM Quantum Compute Service a su funcionamiento normal tras un incidente regional o grave.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Your responsibilities {#your-responsibilities}"
msgstr "Tus responsabilidades {#your-responsibilities}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a regional failure occurs, IBM recommends the following course of action.\n"
msgstr "Si se produce un fallo regional, IBM recomienda el siguiente curso de acción.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Switch to an alternate region (recommended)**\n"
msgstr "**Cambiar a una región alternativa (recomendado)**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If your workload allows it, provision a new IBM Quantum Compute Service [instance](/guides/instances) in the alternate region and resubmit any impacted jobs there. This is the fastest path to resuming operations.\n"
msgstr "Si tu carga de trabajo lo permite, aprovisiona una nueva [instancia](/guides/instances) de IBM Quantum Compute Service en la región alternativa y reenvía allí los jobs afectados. Es el camino más rápido para reanudar las operaciones.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You might not be able to switch regions if, for example:\n"
msgstr "Es posible que no puedas cambiar de región si, por ejemplo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Your work requires specific qubit characteristics that are only available in the affected region.\n"
msgstr "Tu trabajo requiere características específicas de los qubits que solo están disponibles en la región afectada.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Regulatory or data-residency requirements prevent you from using a different region.\n"
msgstr "Requisitos regulatorios o de residencia de datos te impiden usar una región diferente.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Wait for service recovery in your region**\n"
msgstr "**Esperar a que el servicio se recupere en tu región**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If switching regions is not an option, wait for IBM to recover the service in your region. IBM will communicate status and progress through the [IBM Cloud status page](https://cloud.ibm.com/status). After recovery is confirmed, resubmit any impacted jobs.\n"
msgstr "Si cambiar de región no es una opción, espera a que IBM recupere el servicio en tu región. IBM comunicará el estado y el progreso a través de la [página de estado de IBM Cloud](https://cloud.ibm.com/status). Una vez confirmada la recuperación, reenvía los jobs afectados.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additional responsibilities {#additional-responsibilities}"
msgstr "Responsabilidades adicionales {#additional-responsibilities}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-16
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a full breakdown of IBM and customer responsibilities during a disaster recovery event, see [Disaster recovery](/guides/responsibilities#disaster-recovery) in the Responsibilities topic.\n"
msgstr "Para un desglose completo de las responsabilidades de IBM y del cliente durante un evento de recuperación ante desastres, consulta [Recuperación ante desastres](/guides/responsibilities#disaster-recovery) en el tema Responsabilidades.\n"
